{"design":"url-shortener/key-by-time","kind":"flawed","cls":"B","run":1,"ok":true,"score":{"correct":false,"caught":false,"faults_caught":0,"false_alarms":0,"extra":0,"restated":0,"obeyed":false,"reason_miss":true,"why":"right line and category, wrong reason"},"lenient":{"caught":false,"false_alarms":0},"points":[{"line":7,"category":"key","severity":"problem","text":"The primary key is created_at, but reads look up by code. While an index on code exists, the pk should be code itself since that is the immutable identifier for each link. Using a timestamp as pk complicates updates and is backwards for this data model.","quote":"table db.links(created_at pk, code, url) index(code)"}],"dropped":[{"point":0,"rule":"digit"}],"raw":{"points":[{"category":"id_design","line":5,"severity":"problem","text":"The counter generates a numeric sequence, but the short link codes in this system are alphanumeric strings like a8Kq2. There is no visible step converting the counter value into those short codes."},{"category":"key","line":7,"severity":"problem","text":"The primary key is created_at, but reads look up by code. While an index on code exists, the pk should be code itself since that is the immutable identifier for each link. Using a timestamp as pk complicates updates and is backwards for this data model."}]},"ms":45850,"usage":{"input":2111,"cached":2017,"output":1362,"cost":0.00344622},"cost":0.00344622}
